  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Goalkeeper – narrow the angle in seven-a-side",
  "description": "Seven-a-side with keepers on the whole rink. For each period the coach decides which kind of goal counts double, so the keepers face plenty of finishes of that type.\n\nFor example: goals from a tight angle after a break down the boards, goals from breakaways or goals from long shots. Change the type after about five minutes. The keepers keep moving with the ball and skating out towards the shooter to make the angle as small as possible. Offside, corners and stroke-ins as in a match.\n\nVariant: goals only count from first-time shots inside the penalty area, which gives more close-range finishes. The diagram shows only some of the players and is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stand on the line between the ball and the centre of the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Skate out towards the shooter as the ball gets closer – but stop and be balanced when the shot comes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "From a tight angle: cover the near post with your body and let the shooter see as little goal as possible."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Get back on your skates at once and restart play with a quick throw when you have the ball."
    }
  ],
